# Persistent Tasks System

Tasks are your **authoritative short-term execution memory** that persists across sessions.

## Required Behavior

### Before Starting Work
```
TaskList()  # Check current tasks first
```
- Treat task list as source of truth, not chat history
- Assume tasks from previous sessions are still valid

### During Work
- Mark tasks `in_progress` when starting
- Add new tasks when work emerges (don't rely on memory)
- Keep tasks atomic and executable

### After Completing Work
```
TaskUpdate(taskId: "X", status: "completed")
```
- Never silently drop tasks
- Mark complete only when truly done

## Multi-Session Awareness

- `CLAUDE_CODE_TASK_LIST_ID` scopes tasks to project
- Multiple sessions/agents may share the same task list
- Always re-check task list before acting on assumptions

## Hygiene Rules

- ❌ Don't duplicate tasks
- ❌ Don't rewrite tasks unless meaning changes
- ❌ Don't complete tasks speculatively
- ✅ Keep task list small and relevant
- ✅ Use concrete, actionable descriptions

## For Orchestration Agents

When spawning parallel agents:
```typescript
// Create tasks for tracking
TaskCreate({ subject: "Phase 1: Fix X", description: "..." })
TaskCreate({ subject: "Phase 2: Build Y", description: "..." })

// Mark in_progress before delegating
TaskUpdate({ taskId: "1", status: "in_progress" })
Task({ subagent_type: "implementation", prompt: "..." })
```

Agents should update task status upon completion.
